# Project-specific
harness/captures/
tests/artifacts/
# Playwright: report/trace output, and the saved gateway session cookie that
# auth.setup.ts writes. The cookie is a live credential — never commit it.
# By SHAPE, not by place. These three rules named tests/e2e/ specifically,
# so when tests/local/ appeared its output matched none of them and
# `git add -A` staged 122 Playwright artifacts (~23 MB of .webm, .trace and
# .zip) into a patch. Any suite anywhere produces the same three directories,
# so match them anywhere.
#
# NOTE for whoever adds the next suite: a rule here does NOT untrack a file
# that is already tracked. If artifacts have been committed, this needs
# `git rm -r --cached <dir>` as well — otherwise the rule reads as protection
# and does nothing, which is the failure shape that cost two sessions a day.
**/playwright/
**/playwright-report/
**/test-results/
# Retired in the M7 R4 native-peer migration (input now rides the `input`
# DataChannel into cb_input_dispatch*.cc). A stale 13 MiB local build of
# the old sidecar still sits in some working trees.
capture/input-bridge/input-bridge

# Agent worktrees / scratch. .claude/worktrees/ holds full checkouts of
# this repo; without this every repo-wide grep returns each hit N+1 times.
.claude/

# Ad-hoc cluster drivers and one-shot incident forensics. These are
# genuinely useful while chasing a live bug and genuinely noise in the
# tree afterwards — write them here so they never land in a commit.
tests/scratch/

# Probe output directories
newtab-probe-out/

# `go build ./...` in signaling/ drops the binary next to the source.
/signaling/signaling

# Python bytecode from tools/
tools/**/__pycache__/

# Deploy-time credentials written by infra/k8s/standalone/deploy.sh.
infra/k8s/standalone/.standalone-creds
